  "notes": [
    "When you introduce someone, Hindi uses the respectful plural: ये मेरे दोस्त रवि हैं (\"this my friend Ravi are\"), रवि जयपुर से हैं. The same हैं works for a man or a woman.",
    "मेरे / मेरी follows the friend: मेरे दोस्त for a man, मेरी दोस्त for a woman. करते / करती works the same way.",
    "इनका नाम ___ है (\"their name is\") is the polite way to say his or her name. It does not change for a man or a woman.",
    "आपका स्वागत है means \"you are welcome here\". It is not the reply to thank you."
  ]
